# Expert-bias reward check (user 2026-11-06: "run debugging and see if the
# expert behavior scores the best reward").
#
# Both fine-tune critics, SAC run F (step 50k) and IQL run E2 (step 100k),
# rate "steer more left, less throttle" above the expert's own action in every
# recorded expert state: Q rises steadily toward the -0.4 offsets in 100% of
# 1,995 states (critic_slope.py). Does the TRAINING REWARD agree? The expert
# drives the same 40 seeded Town05 episodes (goal and explore by seed parity)
# unbiased and with a constant EXPERT_BIAS on every executed action, and each
# episode logs its return under this reward (il_record.env -> il_expert.env, the
# fine-tunes' reward). Dry: nothing saved, no DART noise, no coverage bursts.
# Each variant overlay sources this one and sets only EXPERT_BIAS.
. "$REPO/slurm/il_record.env"
export EXPERT_RECORD_DRY=1 EXPERT_RECORD_EPISODES=40
